<description>
Move each interior marker to the cell just inside the matching-color frame side.

Input structure
The grid has background-colored corners, a one-cell rectangular frame, and a
background interior containing colored marker pixels.

Rule
Clear the frame interior. If an interior marker has the top, bottom, left, or
right frame-side color, repaint it just inside that side while preserving its
original column or row. Interior colors not used by any frame side disappear.

Key insight
The four side colors are directional labels, so each marker's color selects
the target side and its orthogonal coordinate supplies the placement.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "colored marker pixel s inside the rectangular frame",
  "dst": "inner-edge slot d adjacent to a frame side",
  "match_cond": "s.color equals d's frame-side color; top/bottom slots keep s.column and left/right slots keep s.row",
  "transform": "clear the frame interior to bg; paint matched markers at d and delete marker colors absent from the frame"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-17 rows x 10-17 cols
  background: 0 (black)
  frame:
    shape: 1-cell-wide rectangular border spanning entire grid edge
    corners: bg (all four corner cells are background)
    sides: 4 distinct non-bg colors; top/bottom rows uniform, left/right cols uniform
  markers:
    location: scattered single pixels in the interior (rows 1..H-2, cols 1..W-2)
    matching: 5-10 markers whose color equals one of the 4 frame-side colors
    distractors: 1-3 markers whose color is not any frame-side color [observed]
    no_collision: two same-side markers never share the projected coordinate
      (top/bottom markers have unique columns; left/right markers have unique rows)
    per_side_count: 0-3 per side; at least 3 of the 4 sides have >=1 marker [observed]
  output:
    frame preserved; interior cleared to bg
    each matching marker moves to the cell just inside its matching frame side,
      keeping its orthogonal coordinate (top/bottom keep column, left/right keep row)
    distractor markers are deleted

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims H in [10,17], W in [10,17].
    2. Choose 4 distinct non-bg colors for top/bottom/left/right frame sides.
    3. Build the frame (uniform sides, bg corners).
    4. Decide per-side marker counts (0-3 each, total matching 5-10).
    5. For each side, pick distinct valid coordinates for output positions
       (top-side -> unique cols in [1,W-2]; left-side -> unique rows in [1,H-2]; etc.).
       Place matching markers at output positions (just inside the frame side).
    6. For each output marker, pick a random interior position to be its input location
       (same col for top/bottom markers, same row for left/right markers, but interior
       row/col chosen randomly from [1,H-2] or [1,W-2]). Ensure no two input markers
       share a cell.
    7. Add 1-3 distractor markers at unused interior cells with colors outside
       the 4 frame colors.
    8. Clear output interior to bg, place output markers at their target positions.
```
