       Compute num_layers = cycles * P, total_rows = num_layers + W - 1,
       plateau = total_rows - 2*grow (must be >=2; adjust grow/cycles if not).
    3. Size grid to fit all bands + marker row with margin.
    4. Place marker at row 1: P random unique non-grey non-black colors.
    5. Place each band (top-left anchor), draw the parallelogram shape,
       fill with palette cycling by layer to get the output.
    6. Input = output with all band pixels replaced by grey (5).
